[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Ideal Servant]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.31]Lesson 49 | 第49课
[00:02.34]The ideal servant | 理想的仆人
[00:09.90]What was Bessie's 'little weakness' ? | 贝西的“小毛病”是什么？
[00:14.96]It is a good thing my aunt Harriet died years ago. | 我的姑妈哈丽特多年前去世，这是件好事。
[00:18.97]If she were alive today she would not be able to air her views on her favourite topic of conversation: domestic servants. | 如果她活到今天，就无法在她最喜欢的话题——家仆——上大发议论了。
[00:29.25]Aunt Harriet lived in that leisurely age when servants were employed to do housework. | 哈丽特姑妈生活在那个雇人干家务活的悠闲年代。
[00:35.42]She had a huge, rambling country house called 'The Gables'. | 她有一幢叫“山墙庄园”的宽敞而凌乱的大乡间宅邸。
[00:40.36]She was sentimentally attached to this house, | 她对这幢房子怀有深厚的感情，
[00:43.82]for even though it was far too big for her needs, she persisted in living there long after her husband's death. | 因为尽管它远远超出了她的需要，丈夫去世后她仍执意长期住在那里。
[00:52.82]Before she grew old, aunt Harriet used to entertain lavishly. | 在年迈之前，哈丽特姑妈惯于大摆宴席。
[00:57.84]I often visited The Gables when I was a boy. | 我小时候常去“山墙庄园”做客。
[01:01.45]No matter how many guests were present, the great house was always immaculate. | 无论来了多少客人，这幢大房子总是收拾得纤尘不染。
[01:07.62]The parquet floors shone like mirrors; | 镶木地板亮得像镜子；
[01:10.94]highly polished silver was displayed in gleaming glass cabinets; | 擦得锃亮的银器陈列在闪闪发光的玻璃柜里；
[01:16.31]even my uncle's huge collection of books was kept miraculously free from dust. | 甚至连姑父收藏的大量书籍也奇迹般的一尘不染。
[01:23.38]Aunt Harriet presided over an invisible army of servants that continuously scrubbed, cleaned, and polished. | 哈丽特姑妈统率着一支看不见的仆人大军，他们不停地擦洗、清扫和抛光。
[01:32.83]She always referred to them as 'the shifting population', | 她总是把他们称作“流动人口”，
[01:37.88]for they came and went with such frequency that I never even got a chance to learn their names. | 因为他们来去如此频繁，我甚至从来没有机会记住他们的名字。
[01:45.56]Though my aunt pursued what was, in those days an enlightened policy, | 尽管姑妈奉行着当时算是开明的政策，
[01:51.26]in that she never allowed her domestic staff to work more than eight hours a day, she was extremely difficult to please. | 从不让家仆每天工作超过8小时，她却极难取悦。
[02:00.28]While she always criticized the fickleness of human nature, | 虽然她总是批评人性的变化无常，
[02:04.95]she carried on an unrelenting search for the ideal servant to the end of her days, | 却直到去世前一刻都在不懈地寻找理想的仆人，
[02:12.10]even after she had been sadly disillusioned by Bessie. | 即使在被贝西伤心地断送了幻想之后也是如此。
[02:17.29]Bessie worked for aunt Harriet for three years. | 贝西为哈丽特姑妈干了3年。
[02:21.04]During that time she so gained my aunt's confidence, that she was put in charge of the domestic staff. | 在此期间，她深得姑妈的信任，被提拔主管家仆。
[02:29.03]Aunt Harriet could not find words to praise Bessie's industriousness and efficiency. | 哈丽特姑妈不知该怎么夸贝西的勤勉和能干才好。
[02:36.05]In addition to all her other qualifications, Bessie was an expert cook. | 除了其他种种能耐之外，贝西还是个烹调好手。
[02:42.10]She acted the role of the perfect servant for three years before Aunt Harriet discovered her 'little weakness'. | 她完美地扮演了3年理想仆人的角色，直到哈丽特姑妈发现了她的“小毛病”。
[02:50.67]After being absent from The Gables for a week, | 姑妈离开“山墙庄园”一周之后，
[02:53.84]my aunt unexpectedly returned one afternoon with a party of guests and instructed Bessie to prepare dinner. | 一天下午带着一批客人出人意料地回来了，并吩咐贝西准备晚餐。
[03:02.21]Not only was the meal well below the usual standard, but Bessie seemed unable to walk steadily. | 饭菜远低于平时的水准不说，贝西似乎还走路不稳。
[03:09.97]She bumped into the furniture and kept mumbling about the guests. | 她撞在家具上，嘴里不停地咕哝着客人们的事。
[03:14.83]When she came in with the last course--a huge pudding--she tripped on the carpet | 当她端上最后一道菜——一个大布丁——时，在地毯上绊了一跤，
[03:21.08]and the pudding went flying through the air, narrowly missed my aunt, and crashed on the dining table with considerable force. | 布丁飞了出去，险些砸中姑妈，然后重重地摔碎在餐桌上。
[03:31.31]Though this caused great mirth among the guests, Aunt Harriet was horrified. | 虽然这使客人们哄堂大笑，哈丽特姑妈却吓坏了。
[03:38.37]She reluctantly came to the conclusion that Bessie was drunk. | 她勉强得出结论：贝西喝醉了。
[03:43.37]The guests had, of course, realized this from the moment Bessie opened the door for them and, long before the final catastrophe, | 客人们当然从贝西为他们开门那一刻起就已看出了这一点，而且早在最后这场灾难之前，
[03:53.35]had had a difficult time trying to conceal their amusement. | 就一直费了好大劲才忍住不笑。
[03:58.04]The poor girl was dismissed instantly. | 可怜的姑娘当即被解雇了。
[04:01.69]After her departure, Aunt Harriet discovered that there were piles of empty wine bottles of all shapes and sizes neatly stacked in what had once been Bessie's wardrobe. | 她走后，哈丽特姑妈发现，在贝西曾经用过的衣柜里，整整齐齐地堆放着各种形状大小的空酒瓶。
[04:14.97]They had mysteriously found their way there from the wine cellar! | 它们神秘地从酒窖弄到了那里！
